<?xml version="1.0"?>
  <aerodynamics>
    <!-- Body + tandem wings + pusher shrouds of the X1 concept model; no control surfaces. Derivatives from an AVL 3.52 vortex-lattice model about the race CG: -->
    <!-- NACA 3409 wings (front low, rear high) with duct-wall end plates, fuselage and sponsons as plan/side plates (slender-body Munk moments), shrouds as ring wings. -->
    <!-- The lift fans' ram drag and the fan thrust changes with body rates come from the propellers (Engines/X1_lift_fan_*.xml). -->
    <!-- CL, CD, Cm vs alpha: AVL linear up to stall at -18/+22 deg (chosen: low-aspect wings with end plates stall late, Hoerner FDL), -->
    <!-- then a flat plate on the solid planform 11.0 m2, fan discs open (CD90 1.17, Hoerner FDD), its centre of pressure moving to the planform centroid at 90 deg -->
    <!-- CD0 0.2759 = CdA 1.32 m2: friction x form factor on the measured wetted areas (Raymer, Hoerner), duct rings as crossflow sections CD 1.0 (NACA TN 3038), pods, wheels, upsweep, +10 % interference (chosen) -->
